SUMMARY:[Grant Radar] Pilot and Feasibility Studies in Preparation for Substance Use and HIV Prevention Intervention and Services Research Trials (R34 Clinical Trial Optional) — due
DESCRIPTION:Three-year R34 grants (up to $450k direct costs in total) for pilot and feasibility work ahead of effectiveness or implementation trials in SUD treatment and recovery services. Pain-co-occurring populations and addiction-workforce training are named priorities. MORE fits as a pilot of a MORE implementation or training strategy (e.g.\, fidelity and workforce capacity in a new setting such as an OTP\, FQHC or treatment court) or an adaptation for an understudied population. Dr. Garland/UCSD would be the likely applicant\, with More Therapy as the training subcontractor\; More Therapy is also eligible to apply directly.\n\nPath: Direct/Sub · Priority 3.0\nhttps://files.simpler.grants.gov/opportunities/3820f2c5-4b44-47ad-8a29-9f6084d60bb2/attachments/ff757909-ab97-4782-8f40-2ba1c9731e1f/PAR-28-093-Full-Announcement.html
